    "title": "Houston Rockets TV Schedule",
    "text": "See how to watch or stream the 2025-26 Houston Rockets season with this local and national TV schedule. (Full NBA schedule available here.) This site may earn a commission on subscriptions purchased via this page. Friday, April 24 Time (UTC)Game / TV12:00 amWestern Conference Quarterfinal4Los Angeles Lakers vs 5Houston RocketsGame 3Prime Video | TSN4Sunday, April 26 Time (UTC)Game / TV1:30 amWestern Conference Quarterfinal4Los Angeles Lakers vs 5Houston RocketsGame 4NBC, PeacockWednesday, April 29 Time (UTC)Game / TVTBDWestern Conference Quarterfinal5Houston Rockets vs 4Los Angeles LakersGame 5 - if necessarytbdFriday, May 1 Time (UTC)Game / TVTBDWestern Conference Quarterfinal4Los Angeles Lakers vs 5Houston RocketsGame 6 - if necessaryTBDSunday, May 3 Time (UTC)Game / TVTBDWestern Conference Quarterfinal5Houston Rockets vs 4Los Angeles LakersGame 7 - if necessaryTBD No more upcoming games to show. How to Watch Houston Rockets Games Now featuring Kevin Durant, the Houston Rockets look to build on last year’s results, which saw them finish second in the West but lose in the first round of the playoffs. The networks certainly seem bullish on their chances; Houston is set for 31 nationally televised games this season, including 11 on NBC Sports (highlighted by the season opener against Oklahoma City), ten on ESPN/ABC (highlighted by a Christmas game against the Lakers), seven on Prime Video and three on NBA TV. Locally, Space City Home Network (SCHN) is set for 65 games this season. SCHN is the only local NBA broadcast partner without a dedicated direct-to-subscriber streaming service. Viewing options below: Jan 28, 2025; Atlanta, Georgia, USA; Houston Rockets forward Jae’Sean Tate (8) does an interview after a victory over the Atlanta Hawks at State Farm Arena. Mandatory Credit: Brett Davis-Imagn Images Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (Space City Home Network): NBA League Pass (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games, plus NBA TV. Also available as a standalone purchase through Amazon Prime Video. National games (ESPN/ABC, NBC/Peacock and Prime Video): Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Amazon Prime Video: All Amazon-produced games on Prime Video, plus the ability to purchase NBA League Pass as an add-on. Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $100 off YouTube TV ($20 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3); NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network, plus Space City Home Network. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network, plus Space City Home Network; NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network, plus Space City Home Network on DirecTV, Xfinity, UVerse and more (but not Dish). Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. In-Person See the Rockets in person at the Toyota Center, or catch them on the road, by purchasing tickets from Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
